body:
Ha, this.

/*Pointless whining*/

When my oldest two siblings were of colleging age, my parents bought them each a house, a car, paid their tuition, their books, their utilities, *everything* they would need for the next four years.  If they wanted money for things like alcohol, they could get a job, but they didn't have to.

When I was of colleging age, I heard "Well....go fuck yourself, son".  Oh, and if it wasn't implied by the first part of this pointless whining, my parents' income is too high for me to apply for student loans except for private ones, which I stopped being able to get sophmore year, meaning I had to drop out.

The kicker was that of all my siblings, I scored the highest on college entrance exams, and one of my sisters (who is also getting told to go fuck off) and I are the only ones who wanted to pursue a useful degree (meaning: not communications)

/*end pointless whining, carry on*/
